<title>TURKEY: Turkish C/A deficit rises to $4.4 bln in 1996.</title>
<headline>Turkish C/A deficit rises to $4.4 bln in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's current account gave a deficit of $4.39 billion in 1996, up from $2.34 billion a year ago, the central bank said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said the deficit including Turkey's unregistered earnings from the &quot;suitcase trade&quot; was $1.45 billion in 1996.</p>
